@cc [owner:flvndvd,label:product] frame-lint-diagnostics
Lint MUST check the Frame folder with the Viz declarations and report source file, line and column
diagnostics. The standard layout reserves functions/ and databases/ for backend code and excludes
them from UI linting. Type errors, lint errors and missing tooling MUST fail the command.

@cc [owner:flvndvd,label:product] frame-lint-tailwind-classes
Quoted className attributes, literal branches of conditional or logical className expressions,
and literal arguments or object keys in cn, clsx or classnames calls MUST fail linting when they
contain forbidden Tailwind utilities such as h-[600px]. Interpolated values inside utility brackets
in className template strings MUST also fail. Comments, display text and style props MUST NOT
trigger this rule. Diagnostics MUST report file, line and column and identify the offending class.

@cc [owner:flvndvd,label:product] frame-lint-project-files
The script MUST NOT modify or execute Frame source or replace existing project configs. It MUST
lint the current source with its standard configs, even when the project has its own configs.

@cc [owner:flvndvd,label:product] frame-lint-package-file-refs
String literals and templates without interpolation in UI and backend source MUST fail linting
when they reference an existing file inside the Frame package via its absolute scoped path.
Diagnostics MUST include file, line, column and the portable ./ path to use. Relative paths,
file IDs and references outside the package MUST NOT trigger this rule. Package membership MUST
be checked from the local source listing without stat calls through GCS Fuse for each reference.

@cc [owner:flvndvd,label:performance] frame-lint-local-files
The checker files MUST be cached on local sandbox disk after first use. Generated lint configs
MUST stay on local disk and MUST be removed when the lint command exits.

@cc [owner:flvndvd,label:product] frame-lint-function-refs
When manifest.json exists, UI calls to useFrameFunction, useFrameFunctionMutation and their legacy
usePodFunction counterparts imported from @dust/react-hooks MUST fail linting if a literal string
or template without interpolation names a function absent from manifest.functions. Aliased and
namespace imports MUST be checked. Diagnostics MUST include file, line, column and declared names.
Computed names, shadowed bindings and imports from other modules MUST NOT trigger this rule.
Frames without a manifest MUST skip this check.

@cc [owner:flvndvd,label:security] frame-types-verified-cache
Downloaded archives MUST match the manifest checksum and size before extraction. A cache entry
MUST become visible only after extraction succeeds. A changed manifest id MUST select new types.
